    "media:imagetext": "May\nEighteenth,\n1 9 2 7\nW. H. Howard Estate Co.,\nSharon B1dg.,\nSan Francisco.\nGentlemen:\nThe City of San Francisco for some time past has been\nendeavoring to secure a suitable tract of land for municipal air\nport purposes.\nWe had under investigation sites at South San Francisco,\nM111brae, South of San Mateo and lands under water at San Mateo\nPoint easterly of your property.\nWe found that it would be\nimpracticable to select a permanent site until we had gathered\nsufficient data in regara to the fog and wind conditions, as this\ndata is not available at the present time.\nWe finally leased from the Mills Estate a temporary field\nfor a period of three years, with the privilege of extension of an\nadditional two years.\nIt is our idea to establish small meteorological stations\non or near sites under contemplation, and to ascertain the fog and\nwind conditions over a period of twelve months.\nThe work will be\nin charge of men assigned to us by the United States Weather Bureau.\nWe contemplate the construction of the necessary building immediately\nand the period of observation would extend from July 1, 1927 to June\nsecuring permission from your Company.\noi course,\nould be made revocable on thirty days! notice in the event of the\nsale of the property, and we would remove trom your property the\nbuilding when we vacated the same.\nI am also enclosing map marked file 4-7732, giving full\ndetails\noi the location and construction work.\nThanking you in advance for any courtesies you may extend\nto us in this matter, I am\nVery truly yours,\nJJP:KA\nRIGHT OF WAY AGENT.\n2Sa 0la.\n810",
